# Hacker House Goa 2026 — Frame & ID Generator

A single-file, no-build web app built against the official shortlisting brief. It implements
**both** formats so you can pick whichever fits your post:

- **ID Card** — photo + name/handle/org/city/role + a generated "Builder Title", laid out like
  an event badge (terminal/dossier style, 4 selectable colorways).
- **PFP Frame** — the same photo cropped into a circular, ring-branded frame ready to use as an
  X profile picture.

Everything runs client-side. No backend, no login, no upload wait.

## How it meets the brief

| Requirement | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| Upload JPG/PNG/HEIC | Native file input + drag-drop. HEIC/HEIF (iPhone) is converted in-browser on demand via `heic2any`, loaded only when needed. |
| Handles real photos (any crop/aspect) | Cover-fit + drag-to-reposition + zoom slider + **pinch-to-zoom** on touch, so off-center or oddly-cropped photos can always be framed correctly. |
| Near-instant result | Everything is drawn on a `<canvas>` in the browser — no server round trip, no loading screen. |
| On-brand | Custom "identity system" visual language (not a logo pasted on a generic badge): generated ID code, decorative scan/QR block, circular stamp seal, coordinates, dashed ticket lines, 4 curated colorways. |
| Downloadable real file | "Download PNG" renders the card at 2× resolution (2160×2160) via an offscreen canvas and saves a real `.png`. |
| Working share flow | "Share to X" uses the **Web Share API** with the exported image file — on supporting phones (Android Chrome, iOS Safari) this opens the native share sheet with X as a target and the image **already attached**, plus a pre-filled caption with `#FrameInGoa`. Where the browser doesn't support sharing files (most desktops today), it falls back to downloading the PNG and opening a pre-filled X compose window, with an on-screen note asking the user to attach the file. |
| Mobile-friendly | Responsive single-column layout under ~920px, touch-first drag/pinch controls, all tap targets sized for thumbs. |
| No login/signup wall | None — the tool works fully in one pass. |

### About the "OG image" fallback path
This is a static site with no backend, so there's nowhere to host a per-user dynamic Open Graph
image for a shareable link. The Web Share API path (direct image attach) is the practical
equivalent for a client-only build and is what most mobile users will hit. If you want true
link-preview sharing later, the natural upgrade is a small serverless function (e.g. a Vercel
Edge Function) that accepts the canvas data and returns a page with a matching `og:image` —
not required for this submission, but flagged here as the next step.

## Run it locally
Just open `index.html` in a browser.

## Deploy — pick one

### Vercel (recommended — fastest)
```bash
npm i -g vercel
vercel
```
No build command needed, it's static. You'll get a link like `https://hhgoa-frame.vercel.app`.

### Netlify
Drag the project folder onto [app.netlify.com/drop](https://app.netlify.com/drop), or:
```bash
npm i -g netlify-cli
netlify deploy --prod
```

### GitHub Pages
```bash
git init && git add . && git commit -m "HH Goa 2026 frame generator"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<you>/hhgoa-frame.git
git push -u origin main
```
Then **Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch → main / (root)**.

## Submission checklist (per the brief)

1. Deploy and open your live link.
2. Upload a photo, fill in your details, pick a colorway, and pick ID Card or PFP Frame.
3. Tap **Share to X** (attaches the image directly on supported phones) or **Download PNG**
   and attach it manually, then post — the caption already includes `#FrameInGoa`.
4. Confirm the post is live and actually contains `#FrameInGoa` (submissions without it are
   invalid per the brief).
5. Submit via the form: https://forms.gle/jM5hTaGvsrfEfixPA — one submission per team.
6. Deadline: **11:59 PM, 13 August 2026**.